The program pulls every `name <- value` assignment out of the input in order, so any surrounding prose is ignored. If the value is an integer, it is stored directly. If it is a variable name, that variable's current value is copied. At the end it prints the three variables in the requested format.

```python
import re
import sys

def main():
    text = sys.stdin.read()
    env = {}
    pattern = re.compile(r'([A-Za-z_]\w*)\s*<-\s*(-?\d+|[A-Za-z_]\w*)')
    for target, src in pattern.findall(text):
        if re.fullmatch(r'-?\d+', src):
            env[target] = int(src)
        else:
            env[target] = env.get(src)
    print("a ?= {}; b ?= {}; TMP ?= {};".format(env.get('a'), env.get('b'), env.get('TMP')))

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```
